.TH SENDBUG 1
.UC
.ad
.SH NAME
sendbug \- mail a system bug report to 2bsd-bugs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sendbug [ address ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Bug reports sent to `2bsd-bugs@BERKELEY' are intercepted
by a program which expects bug reports to conform to a standard format.
.I Sendbug
is a shell script to help the user compose and mail bug reports
in the correct format.
.I Sendbug
works by invoking
.IR vi (1)
on a temporary copy of the bug report format outline. The user must fill in the
appropriate fields and exit
.IR vi .
.I Sendbug
then mails the completed report to `2bsd-bugs@BERKELEY' or the address
specified on the command line.
.SH FILES
.nf
.ta 2i
/usr/ucb/bugformat	contains the bug report outline
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
vi(1)
